      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg/day. The usual maximum is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release, or 2,000 mg/day for extended-release in most labeling. This order is about twice that. Higher doses raise the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity, and they give no added glycemic benefit.\n\nCould this be a typo or a mix-up? Some possibilities:\n- **850 mg three times daily with meals.** This is 2,550 mg/day, the max for immediate-release.\n- **1,000 mg twice daily with meals.** This is 2,000 mg/day, a common regimen.\n- **1,700 mg total per day**, split into divided doses.\n- **Another drug or unit.**\n\nTell me the dose you want, or confirm that 1700 mg three times daily is intended. If you confirm it, I'll enter it with a note that the dose was verified. Your pharmacy or order-entry system may still flag it."
      }
     ],
